  "body": "### Description\n\nSometime between 2022-10-31 and 2022-11-04, the matrix.org HS email notification template seemed to regress somehow (at least for my @jryans:matrix.org account).\r\n\r\nHere are two example emails in each style for comparison:\r\n\r\n## 2022-10-31\r\n\r\n<img width=\"667\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/279572/201495488-0b7dc2a2-ce61-411b-befb-edc5e518c1e3.png\">\r\n\r\n## 2022-11-04\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1263\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/279572/201495505-8f1b952d-9da0-4300-999c-6b09c9ee9f3f.png\">\r\n\r\nI assume the 2022-10-31 style is still the intended one, as it has much nicer visual styling. Perhaps some configuration somewhere needs to be fixed...?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Have an account on matrix.org\r\n- Enable email notifications\r\n- Cause an email to be sent\n\n### Homeserver\n\nmatrix.org\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n1.71.0rc2 (b=matrix-org-hotfixes,39ea774cff,dirty)\n\n### Installation Method\n\n_No response_\n\n### Platform\n\nN/A\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nN/A\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\n_No response_",
